WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.600
So today I want to announce a new project, but first I have to begin by explaining that for the last couple

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.940
years, I have been the manager of a fictional soccer team called the Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.100
The Swoodilypoopers are led by two time lords, both named John Green, who are married to each other,

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:18.060
and everything was going swimmingly, but then I got obsessed with recreating the past, like Gatsby, and I got fired.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.480
And now after careful consideration, I've decided to retire from semi-professional FIFA playing,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.820
and I'd like to take this opportunity to announce that I will no longer be supporting my family, in part, by playing video game soccer.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.920
However, Hank, there's a couple things you need to understand about English football.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.420
First, if you're in the major leagues of English soccer, which is called the Premier League,

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.480
and you have a really bad season, and you finish in the bottom three, you don't get to play in the Premier League next year,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.520
you are relegated to the league below that, which, helpfully, is called the championship.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.840
You know, because it doesn't feature any of the champions.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.400
Anyway, in every league, the top teams get promoted up each season,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.240
and the bottom teams get relegated down to the league below.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.620
And if you get relegated from the fourth tier, which is helpfully called League Two,

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.340
then you are no longer in the football league, and your team is not even in FIFA anymore.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:05.180
This makes English football fun, and also terrifying, because there is a lot at stake every season for every team.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.020
And no team experience these crazy highs and lows more than Wimbledon FC,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.700
which, for most of its history, was in the lower leagues, but then had a run in the top flight,

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.300
and I mean, they won the FA cup in 1988.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.340
Now, the other big difference between English football and American sports is that there are no franchises.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.960
So like, rich owners can't just move the Dodgers from Brooklyn to Los Angeles because they wanna.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.880
Except occasionally, when they can.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:33.600
In 2002, Wimbledon FC was moved to Milton Keynes, leaving thousands of Wimbledon fans without a club.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.580
I mean, they had a hundred years of history, and then nothing.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:41.540
Their stadium was torn down, their FA cup was sent to Milton Keynes, although was later returned.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.340
So these fans responded by starting a club from scratch: AFC Wimbledon.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.180
And they started in 2002 in the ninth tier of English football.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:52.800
But then they went on this amazing run, and just nine years later, in 2011,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.560
their captain, Danny Kedwell, found himself with one penalty kick to send Wimbledon to the football league.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:05.980
It's Danny Kedwell, deep breaths, deep breaths, deep breaths, come on, Danny, this, for league two, it's Danny Kedwell.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.160
Yeah! (screaming and laughing)

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.000
We did it! Aaah, they did it!

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.780
So, AFC Wimbledon became a league two team, which means that you can play them in FIFA.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.580
Last year, they almost got relegated, but then in the last game, they won heroically.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:28.560
In the corner, Jason. Yeah! (screaming)

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.160
Hank, AFC Wimbledon is a truly extraordinary football club.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.260
It's owned and run by its fans, I mean, there's no big money behind it,

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.540
their chairman is a retired accountant.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:42.020
They were the first club in England to have a "Football Fans Against Homophobia" banner at a game,

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.180
basically, Hank, it's the most awesome football club in the world,

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:49.120
and I want to help them stay in the football league, so I'm going to play with them in FIFA 14.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.620
But, I'm going to keep my vow not to be a professional FIFA player anymore,

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:57.740
instead, all ad revenue from the videos will go to sponsor the actual, real AFC Wimbledon team.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:02.640
We're going to have billboards in the stadium and ads in the program, all designed by Nerdfighters,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.280
and hopefully, we're going to help this team that mirrors the values of Nerdfighteria stay in the football league,

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.220
so I can play with them in FIFA 15, and FIFA 16, and beyond, and maybe one day, we can send them to the Premier League.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.980
Now, that might be dreaming, but in 2002, when AFC Wimbledon was playing away games

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.520
in front of 80 fans, it took some dreaming to imagine a world in which they would be a team that you could play in FIFA.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.680
So, Nerdfighters, if you want to help, please subscribe to HankGames and watch the videos.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.560
You can click on my face or there's a link in the dooblydoo.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.940
And let's start designing some ads together, there's more info below,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.220
where you can also find videos of ACF Wimbledon's short but glorious history.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:37.800
So, Hank, I hope you like this new little project. DFTBA, I'll see you on Friday.

